{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"Code review found a correctness defect in the planned design and it has been remediated. The plan had TemporalStarter.start raise UnresolvableBaseBranch with _start catching it around ctx.ledger.run_once. That raise happens inside the _launch effect, after ctx.execution_seeder.seed and after the task snapshot capture. PostgresSideEffectLedger.reserve only returns replayed=True for a _COMPLETED row, and its insert uses on_conflict_do_nothing, so an effect that raises leaves the key _PENDING forever. Every later reconcile pass would re-run _launch, seeding another execution and capturing another snapshot for as long as the branch stayed unresolvable. The remediation validates the declared branch before the ledger effect runs. A new IntakeBaseResolver protocol exposes resolve_base, IntakeContext carries an optional base_resolver, and TemporalStarter implements it over the same remote_head call. Both production wiring sites pass the starter as the resolver. _start now holds the ticket before any seeding. The starter raise is retained as a guard for contexts with no resolver wired. Scope is unchanged, an undeclared ticket still uses github_default_base_branch and is never held by this path."},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789496548764156001,"uuid":"d6479d4c-3d9a-4eaa-8c93-e3f30671d768"}